  "char/4 proxy calibration: run a real tokenizer (cl100k_base or claude equivalent) on a stratified 10% subsample across R, A, TX, TH, U categories and report per-category chars/tok ratios. theory_skeptic correctly notes JSON/code/base64 tokenize at ~2.5-3.5 chars/tok vs prose ~4 chars/tok, meaning the char/4 proxy may systematically UNDER-count R in true tokens (which would RAISE the result-share, strengthening the claim — but the direction must be empirically confirmed, not assumed). Cheap to do, closes the gap permanently.",
