PRIOR_ART_ADEQUATE: no
RATIONALE: Unanimous 5/5 yellow. The measurement is REAL: conservative D1 result-share CC 0.657 (LB95 0.569) / Codex 0.770 (LB95 0.748) with monotone denominator robustness, HHI 0.166/0.016 both below 0.20, session-median corroboration (0.573/0.757 both >0.50), top-decile and Gini heavy-tail metrics with CIs, and cross-instrument replication at |d|=0.113 < 0.40. Pre-registration integrity is accepted: HEAD 8e60c29 LOCK-TS before measurement, frozen operational definitions, D1 remained the conservative headline, the s7 borderline-gate reconciliation (premeasure 0.498-0.502 → locked 0.569) is attributed to clean bucketing under frozen defs not threshold movement. All 9 mandatory fixes and 2 baselines from the design committee were honored. The cost-weighting negative (RE-A4: R-$share collapses to 0.198/0.025 at 10x/100x) is honestly reported as SECONDARY and pre-empts the dollar-story misread — product_realist correctly notes this is a characterization contribution not a cost-optimization result, which is the correct reading. No reviewer found a fatal prior-art collision: DistServe/SplitWise ASSUME the mix, RadixAttention/vLLM-APC/Sarathi cache uniformly, Parrot/Autellix schedule but don't measure. The granular R/A/TX/TH/U/O decomposition + heavy-tail quantification + cross-instrument replication on real agent tool-loops is a genuine gap in the cited literature.

I cannot emit GREEN for three reasons, each independently sufficient under committee rules:

(1) PRIOR-ART SEARCH INCOMPLETE. novelty_killer explicitly reports the mandated live ≥2-source independent novelty sweep was tooling-blocked. The "first granular ... never MEASURES" superlative is uncertified. Additionally, Mooncake (2407.00079) — which characterizes real Kimi production traces and prefix-cache hot-spot reuse — is directly adjacent to the "heavy-tail = cacheable hot spots" framing and is absent from the 8-work cited list. BurstGPT (2401.17644) and the agent-context-compression literature (MemGPT-style) are also uncited. These are scoping gaps, not collisions, but the related-work section must survive a reviewer who knows these papers.

(2) ON-NODE CHAT BASELINE MISSING (unanimous 5/5). The central "reframes which knob governs agent inference" framing rests on an agent-vs-chat structural contrast. The agent side is measured with char/4; the chat side is sourced from published true-token numbers. This is an instrumentation mismatch (evaluation_prosecutor), an instrument-inconsistent central comparison (theory_skeptic), and an incomplete systems validation (systems_reviewer). The fix is straightforward: run the same pipeline over ShareGPT or equivalent. If the chat regime shows result-share << 0.50 under the same methodology, the structural contrast is validated. If chat also shows high prefill share (from long prompts), the "reframes" framing needs honest scoping. Either outcome is publishable; the current gap is not.

(3) CHAR/4 PROXY UNVALIDATED (evaluation_prosecutor + theory_skeptic). The claim that char/4 is "tokenizer-invariant for shares" requires that all component categories have approximately equal chars-per-token ratios. theory_skeptic correctly identifies they don't: JSON/code/structured dumps (dominant in R) tokenize at ~2.5-3.5 chars/tok; natural English prose (dominant in TX) at ~4 chars/tok. The likely direction of the bias STRENGTHENS the claim (R is under-counted by char/4, so true-token R-share is probably higher), but "likely strengthens" is not "verified." A tokenizer calibration on a 10% stratified subsample would either confirm the headline or provide a correction factor. This is cheap and should have been done.

theory_skeptic's point that heavy-tailedness is theoretically EXPECTED for mixtures of bounded prompts and unbounded external I/O is well-taken — the framing should be "quantified a known-expected property at specific magnitudes with CIs and cross-instrument replication" not "discovered heavy-tailedness." This is a presentation/scoping adjustment, not a kill.

product_realist's observation that the cost-share collapse (RE-A4) means no immediate production deployment win is correct but already honestly scoped by the researcher (FIX-1, reported SECONDARY). The characterization stands as a characterization; it does not need to be a cost story.

DISPOSITION: Real measurement, real contribution, three closable gaps. Close (1) by completing the prior-art sweep + citing Mooncake/BurstGPT/context-compression. Close (2) by running an on-node chat baseline. Close (3) by a tokenizer calibration subsample. All are L0-feasible (no new infrastructure, no production access needed). Upon closing, this is a strong green candidate — 5/5 reviewers accept the measurement is real and no collision was found. (area_chair v001)
